      "vision_vetted": true,
      "vision_by": "pick:claude-sonnet-5",
      "vision_reason": "This is a classic Dan wakemia/wunkirmian ceremonial spoon — an anthropomorphic wooden ladle with a bowl-shaped body, carved human legs, and incised geometric decoration — a form specifically associated with the Dan and their neighbors of Côte d'Ivoire/Liberia/Guinea, given to the most hospitable woman for feasts. The Dan peoples span this cross-border region, so the attribution is consistent with the claimed ethnicity.",
